ing but a punchline  with a 66  critical approval rating on rotten  tomatoes it's the mcu's second worst  ranked film and is often cited as the  worst marvel film it wasn't a bad movie  just a largely forgettable one in fact  does anyone even remember what the plot  was about or who the villain was as  rolling stone said the clutter makes her  head feel like it's about to explode and  not in a good way with wonders upon  wonders instead it seems like arcana  that might show up on the midterm final  the next marvel movie director alan  taylor revealed to collider before the  film's release that part of the reshoot  process was to include more of loki yet  even that didn't manage to save the film  from being one of the mcu's most bland  whoa  costumes a bit much  so tight  for kevin feige eternals was the mcu's  way of paying tribute to the late great  jack kirby unfortunately a number of  critics didn't agree with feige's  thoughts slant magazine's review in  particular pummeled the comparison  saying director chloe zhao ultimately  robs the artist's comic of its sweep by  constantly turning a space opera into a  repetitive character drama on rotten  tomatoes eternals holds a 47  critical approval rating making it the  worst ranked mcu film on the platform  that said there was a disparity in  consensus between the critics and the  viewers as the audience approval sits at  a respectable 78  while it isn't uncommon to see this  happen it proved that eternals might  very well be the mcu's most polarizing  film to date he's wasting our time  after the avengers gobbled up the box  office receipts and went back for  seconds it widened eyes in the  entertainment industry if one property  could be so successful and  practically print money why not tap into  the goodwill and reap similar benefits  across other mediums agents of shield  proved to be the template of the best  way to make an avengers show without the  actual avengers and abc knew it but the  network wanted more 